and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Dina Titus (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Dina Titus seeks another term in a Las Vegas-based district that leans Democratic by about two points, with a national environment that has favored her party this cycle. She holds a cash advantage over Republican Carrie Buck, a state senator who has nonetheless raised nearly $2 million and is regarded as one of the GOP's stronger recruits in Nevada. Independent expenditures on both sides have so far been minimal.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available for the district, so the picture rests on fundamentals, expert ratings, and prediction markets. Most raters call the race Likely Democratic, with several rating it Safe or Solid, and markets give Titus roughly a 94% chance of winning. The race is not competitive on current evidence, though Buck's fundraising keeps it from being rated Safe.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9567, "margin": 11.7}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9528, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9532, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9485, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9231, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9459, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9435, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9451, "margin": 11.0}]}